node_modules/

# Sweep and soak output — results are regenerated, never committed.
# A committed CSV outlives its balance era and gets cited after it is void.
*.csv
reports/*.csv
# The gate runner writes one of these per day (M2): a timing log, not a document.
reports/gates-*.json
debugging/out/
# Smoke output is regenerated on every run; the probe images are not.
reports/smoke-*.png
# Per-view captures the compare sheet stitches. The sheet is the artefact; these
# are its working files, and three of them are 4 MB.
# Gate transcripts a review round writes, and the scratch captures a probe takes
# while somebody is looking at a bug. Seven logs and four PNGs reached `main`
# through one `git add -A` (M5). The artefacts a slice DELIVERS are not here.
reports/review*.log
reports/tmp/
# And the same scratch one directory up: four PNGs a probe wrote during S20 were
# committed here and tracked for eleven days, because the guard named the place
# the leak had been found rather than the shape of it (M12b's sweep).
tmp/
reports/.photo-smoke.png
# `house_shots.mjs` opens a 320x240 page to ask where the houses are before it
# aims the real shots. The answer is the point; the picture is scratch (S9).
reports/.house-shots-probe.png
reports/.traffic-shots-probe.png
reports/.crowd-shots-probe.png
# `civic_shots.mjs` and the ad-hoc probes write these while aiming a shot. The
# answer is the point; the picture is scratch (S1).
reports/.civic-probe.png
reports/.probe.png
reports/.compare-*.png
reports/.sheet-*.png

# Build-step bakes: generated on the dev machine, never committed, guarded by a
# hash pin so a stale bake degrades gracefully instead of corrupting anything.
assets/baked/
client/assets/generated/

# Local saves and room state
saves/
rooms/

# Config with secrets; sanitized templates are committed instead
*.local.json
deploy/secrets/

.DS_Store

# local 
dev-prompts.md
dev-questions.md
reports/gates/
reports/.motion-*.png
reports/.smoke-frozen-*.png
# Every tool's scratch image is a dot-file in reports/ — probes, sweeps, frozen
# pairs. Named one by one they were missed one by one, and bulk commits kept
# them (review round before B9).
reports/.*.png
# The storyboard's frames (F2). 61 PNGs and 15 MB, rewritten whole by every
# `node tools/gates.mjs film` run — working files, like the compare sheet's
# per-view captures. What a film DELIVERS is F3's `media/`, which is committed.
reports/storyboard/

# The box, the key and the deploy script (M12, moved out 2026-10-14). `ops/` is a
# SYMLINK to the private ops repo (game-ops/citygrid/), which holds the systemd
# unit, the nginx block and ssh-deploy.sh — the host's identity and the only
# files on this machine that can change a live box. Every sibling game does the
# same; game-ops/README.md is the mapping. Nothing in `ops/` is ever committed
# here, and a clean checkout simply has no `ops/` at all.
ops
tools/deploy.env
